{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNLSqHgseuTH8jMgNchM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KnME23rfjfCFBWbzpknXr7","name":"mcp__claudetto__patch","input":{"patch":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: PLAN.md\n+# Plan: skip blank-id rows in the importer\n+\n+## Requirement (user's words)\n+\n+\"the importer must skip every row whose id is blank but keep rows whose id is the number zero, and log one line per skipped row with its line number\"\n+\n+## Current state\n+\n+The repo holds only `README.md` (\"importer for rows\"). There is no importer code, language, test runner or logger yet. This plan therefore fixes behaviour and tests, and leaves the file layout until the importer exists.\n+\n+## Behaviour\n+\n+- A row is skipped when its id is blank: the id field is missing, empty, or only whitespace.\n+- A row is kept when its id is the number zero. The raw value `0` is a real id and is not blank. The check must test for blankness explicitly (empty or whitespace string, or null/missing), never by truthiness, because `0` is falsy in many languages.\n+- Each skipped row produces exactly one log line that contains its line number. Kept rows produce no skip line.\n+- Skipping a row does not stop the import. Later rows are still processed.\n+\n+## Decisions\n+\n+Defaults below are assumptions. Change them before implementing if they are wrong.\n+\n+- Line number is the 1-based line in the source file, counting the header line if there is one, so the number matches what an editor shows. For multi-line (quoted) records, use the line where the record starts.\n+- Log line format: `skipped line <N>: blank id`. Logging goes through the importer's existing logger at warning level, or stderr if there is none.\n+- Whitespace-only ids count as blank. Ids such as `00` and `0.0` are not blank and are kept. Whether they should count as \"zero\" is not specified, so they are treated as ordinary non-blank ids.\n+\n+## Steps\n+\n+- Add a `isBlankId` helper with the rule above.\n+- In the row loop, call it before any other processing. On blank, log the line and continue.\n+- Track the source line number in the loop, independent of the count of kept rows.\n+\n+## Tests\n+\n+Each test runs the importer on a small input and checks the returned rows and the captured log output.\n+\n+- Blank id (empty): row skipped, one log line naming its line number.\n+- Whitespace-only id: row skipped, one log line.\n+- Missing id column on a row: row skipped, one log line.\n+- Id `0`: row kept, no log line.\n+- Mixed input (valid, blank, `0`, blank): kept rows are the valid and `0` ones in order, log has exactly two lines with the correct line numbers.\n+- Line numbers account for the header line and for earlier skipped rows.\n+- Input with no blank ids: no log lines.\n+\n+## Open questions for the user\n+\n+- Should whitespace-only ids count as blank? (assumed yes)\n+- Should the line number count the header? (assumed yes)\n+- Where should the log go, and in what format? (assumed logger at warning level, format above)\n*** End Patch\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":123,"cache_read_input_tokens":18438,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":123},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0dd2c4ba-6a9d-4983-9940-8d4c087ef973","uuid":"69dcc8a7-9548-42e9-a26b-82d529af29ba","timestamp":"2026-11-24T19:51:58.556Z","request_id":"req_011ChNLSq9FKhKt3wwpYioBD","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KnME23rfjfCFBWbzpknXr7","display_name":"Patch","server_display_name":"claudetto","tool_name":"patch"}]}
